body_markdown:
Your agents can now use[generative UI cards](https://mastra.ai/reference/agents/channels#generative-ui-cards) in Slack. Turn on` generativeUI` and the agent gets a` render_card` tool that posts rich, native cards to the thread.


Agents in Slack usually reply using long blocks of plain text or markdown, making it difficult to see how numbers compare or change over time. With generative UI, the agent decides how to present the data, using fields for key facts, tables for rows of data, charts for metrics or trends, images, and link buttons that open related pages.


Your browser does not support the video tag.A Deploy Agent in Slack answers with a deploy summary, a bar chart of build times, and a table of shipped commits, followed by the setup code and connecting Slack with Mastra Connect.


You've always been able to post UI cards in Slack by predefining them in code, but before generative UI, each card's structure was fixed in advance. Now, with generative UI, the agent creates the card on the fly, choosing the most suitable UI element for each response.


To render Slack-native UI elements, agents call the` render_card` tool, passing in an object that meets the[json-render](https://json-render.dev/) spec. Mastra can then post responses to the thread using Slack's[Block Kit](https://docs.slack.dev/block-kit/) elements.


## Get started


Install` @json-render/chat` :


Terminal


```text
npm   install   @json-render/chat
```


note


Requires` @mastra/core@1.83.0` or later, added in[PR #29820](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/29820) .


This example uses[Mastra Connect](https://mastra.ai/docs/mastra-platform/connect) to manage the Slack connection on Mastra platform. Add` @json-render/chat` to` bundler.dynamicPackages` and set` generativeUI: true` on the Slack provider:


src/mastra/index.ts


```text
import   {   Mastra   }   from   "  @mastra/core/mastra  "  ;
import   {   channels   }   from   "  @mastra/connect  "  ;
import   {   deployAgent   }   from   "  ./agents/deploy-agent  "  ;


export   const   mastra   =   new   Mastra  ({
agents: { deployAgent },
bundler: {
dynamicPackages: [  "  @json-render/chat  "  ]
},
channels:   await   channels  ({
providers: {
slack: {
providerOptions: { generativeUI:   true   }
}
}
})
});
```


Optionally, name the components you want the agent to use in the agent's instructions:


src/mastra/agents/deploy-agent.ts


```text
import   {   Agent   }   from   "  @mastra/core/agent  "  ;
import   {   Memory   }   from   "  @mastra/memory  "  ;


export   const   deployAgent   =   new   Agent  ({
id:   "  deploy-agent  "  ,
name:   "  Deploy Agent  "  ,
instructions:   `  You report on deploys for the mastra-website project.
Answer every deploy question with one render_card card that includes:


- a title and subtitle
- fields for the key facts
- a table
- a chart
- an image
- link buttons
`  ,
model:   "  mastra/anthropic/claude-opus-5.5  "  ,
memory:   new   Memory  ()
});
```


For more information and full configuration options, see:


- [Generative UI cards](https://mastra.ai/reference/agents/channels#generative-ui-cards)
- [Slack](https://mastra.ai/integrations/channels/slack)
- [Mastra Connect](https://mastra.ai/docs/mastra-platform/connect)
- [Channels overview](https://mastra.ai/docs/capabilities/channels)


Generative UI is still experimental — the API may change between releases.
